1
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:11,590
A Place of Our Own

2
00:00:11,590 --> 00:00:14,730
Ellen, I'd like your opinion.

3
00:00:14,730 --> 00:00:16,930
About what?

4
00:00:16,930 --> 00:00:22,940
Well, Richard and I feel that with a baby coming

5
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:30,190
we need to have our own place to live.

6
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:31,400
Oh.

7
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:32,900
Well, what do you think about Richard and me

8
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:35,650
looking for a small house or an apartment

9
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:39,480
at this point in our lives?

10
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:41,550
We love having you here,

11
00:00:41,550 --> 00:00:42,640
and there is room,

12
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:45,420
and ... and when the baby comes,

13
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:49,610
the baby can stay in your room for a while.

14
00:00:49,610 --> 00:00:57,260
Richard feels we need to find a small house.

15
00:00:57,260 --> 00:01:02,180
I remember when I was pregnant with Richard.

16
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:03,930
Philip and I were living with Grandma and Grandpa.

17
00:01:03,930 --> 00:01:05,030
Philip was a young doctor,

18
00:01:05,030 --> 00:01:09,800
and he kept talking about having a house of our own.

19
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,400
It's natural.

20
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,690
What did you do?

21
00:01:13,690 --> 00:01:16,890
We looked at a lot of houses.

22
00:01:16,890 --> 00:01:18,560
Did you find one?

23
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:19,440
Oh, not at first.

24
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:21,130
We couldn't afford it.

25
00:01:21,130 --> 00:01:25,950
Grandpa wanted to lend us the money to buy one,

26
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:28,050
but Philip is too independent.

27
00:01:28,050 --> 00:01:31,590
He didn't want to borrow any money.

28
00:01:31,590 --> 00:01:33,330
Sounds like Richard.

29
00:01:33,330 --> 00:01:35,040
They're all alike.

30
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:38,950
Richard is a real Stewart.

31
00:01:38,950 --> 00:01:39,850
He's independent,

32
00:01:39,850 --> 00:01:45,960
and sometimes just stubborn.

33
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:48,510
When did you buy a house?

34
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:51,720
After Richard was born.

35
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:52,670
I was teaching music,

36
00:01:52,670 --> 00:01:57,580
and Philip was opening his first medical office.

37
00:01:57,580 --> 00:01:58,770
Where was the house?

38
00:01:58,770 --> 00:02:00,760
Right here in Riverdale.

39
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:04,920
Of course, it was a small house,

40
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:08,540
but just right for us.

41
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:10,980
It's funny. History repeats itself.

42
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:12,590
Now Richard and I are having a baby,

43
00:02:12,590 --> 00:02:14,150
and we probably won't be able to

44
00:02:14,150 --> 00:02:16,830
afford a house right away, either.

45
00:02:16,830 --> 00:02:20,820
Why don't you look at some houses, Marilyn?

46
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:22,980
Good idea. \u597D\u4E3B\u610F\u3002

47
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:26,920
Look in the real-estate section of Sunday's Times.

48
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:28,290
You'll learn a lot.

49
00:02:28,290 --> 00:02:30,050
Maybe we should

50
00:02:30,050 --> 00:02:32,990
speak to a real-estate agent about a house.

51
00:02:32,990 --> 00:02:35,830
And a bank about a mortgage.

52
00:02:35,830 --> 00:02:38,060
I'll talk to Richard about it.

53
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:39,420
I think it's a good idea, Ellen.

54
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:42,670
We can learn a lot by asking.

55
00:02:42,670 --> 00:02:44,920
And if I can be of any help,

56
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:45,890
let me know.

57
00:02:45,890 --> 00:02:46,920
As a matter of fact,

58
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:49,900
my friend Virginia Martinelli is a real-estate agent.

59
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:51,100
Good.

60
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:52,380
You won't believe this,

61
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:56,920
but she sold us our first house and this one.

62
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:57,640
Well, I'll tell Richard,

63
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:06,140
and we'll go to see her.

64
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:10,450
Do you think the skirt length is right, Ellen?

65
00:03:10,450 --> 00:03:13,950
Do you think it's too long?

66
00:03:13,950 --> 00:03:16,760
I think the skirt is just right.

67
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:19,280
Are you planning to attach a train to it?

68
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:23,120
No. No train. Just the dress.

69
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:27,200
But I am going to make a headpiece of lace.

70
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:30,230
That dress is gorgeous.

71
00:03:30,230 --> 00:03:32,220
Thanks, Ellen.

72
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:35,570
And thanks for the advice about the house.

73
00:03:35,570 --> 00:03:38,020
I'll talk to Richard about it

74
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:38,790
the minute he comes home.

75
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:40,450
And remember,

76
00:03:40,450 --> 00:03:43,360
we love having you here.

77
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:46,360
There's no need to rush.
